# harnessed — host-level secrets, resolved from 1Password via varlock.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/harnessed/.env.schema and edit the op:// references.
# Per-service secrets live in ~/.config/<service>/.env.schema
#   (e.g. ~/.config/hindsight/.env.schema for the hindsight sidecar).
# `harnessed` detects these schemas and injects resolved env via `varlock run --`
# at launch; values are NEVER written to the repo, a profile, or an image layer.
#
# DSL reference: https://varlock.dev/env-spec
#
# @plugin(@varlock/1password-plugin@1.2.0)
# @initOp(allowAppAuth=true)
# ---

# --- Supply-chain scanners (see docs/harnessed-design.md §7) ---
# All optional. If unset, harnessed runs only the credential-free scanners
# (osv-scanner + pip-audit). The token-gated scanners below never run during
# `harnessed build` — the build is deliberately credential-free — they run in the
# credentialed pass, which `harnessed rescan <image>` performs (and which `build`
# invokes for you against the image it just built). See docs/guides/secrets.md.

# Snyk API token — used by `snyk test` during `harnessed rescan`.
# @optional @sensitive @example="abcd1234-ef56-7890-..."
SNYK_TOKEN=op(op://Private/SNYK_API_TOKEN/credential)

# Socket.dev API token — used by `socket scan create` during `harnessed rescan`.
# Needs the `full-scans:create` + `packages:list` permissions. Your org slug is derived
# from the token; set SOCKET_CLI_ORG_SLUG only to pin one when the token sees several.
# SOCKET_SECURITY_API_KEY is accepted as a legacy alias, but this name is canonical.
# @optional @sensitive @example="sktsec_abcd1234..."
SOCKET_CLI_API_TOKEN=op(op://Private/SOCKET_API_TOKEN/credential)
